{"w":2400,"h":3390,"lines":[{"t":"Reading","x":0.83138706737337198,"y":0.043942533482636992,"c":1,"h":0.016149633401966401,"w":0.083045183817545665},{"h":0.019019687843885413,"c":1,"w":0.76796712239583331,"t":"Roughly 11,700 years ago, as the most recent ice age ended, the climate became","y":0.091445427934829127,"x":0.082135535211724009},{"t":"significantly warmer and wetter, no doubt making Obi's jungle much thicker. According","x":0.08000695098308265,"y":0.10808783678486777,"w":0.80712320963541662,"h":0.019224736261508446,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"to the researchers, it is no coincidence that around this time the first axes crafted from","y":0.12593629368047643,"w":0.80915822347005206,"h":0.019872822944393631,"x":0.07797062046220446},{"h":0.021170361274111649,"w":0.76201655069986984,"x":0.079979859291311475,"c":1,"y":0.14305631616021341,"t":"stone rather than sea shells appear, likely in response to their heavy-duty use for"},{"y":0.16025641827398462,"w":0.81331929524739588,"t":"clearing and modification of the increasingly dense rainforest. While stone takes about","h":0.020267502326177578,"x":0.079984537818301643,"c":1},{"h":0.018913355689484823,"c":1,"x":0.07802876917189025,"w":0.82546198527018233,"y":0.17876106218175802,"t":"twice as long to grind into an axe compared to shell, the harder material keeps its sharp"},{"h":0.017563409720901868,"x":0.079936419646134127,"y":0.19867267783872034,"w":0.15211451212565102,"t":"edge for longer.","c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.080082142264914183,"w":0.81519505818684901,"y":0.23392330362305813,"h":0.017530184720469744,"t":"Judging by the bones which the researchers unearthed in the Kelo caves, people living"},{"y":0.25116517114081849,"w":0.79891403198242195,"c":1,"t":"there mainly hunted the Rothschild's cuscus, a possum-like creature that still lives on","h":0.020365980030161102,"x":0.080011611133281715},{"t":"Obi today. As the forest grew more dense, people probably used axes to clear patches","x":0.080082135836282098,"y":0.27020648994800478,"h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1,"w":0.81314168294270828},{"w":0.32443532307942713,"x":0.080082133013710949,"c":1,"y":0.28924418615860381,"t":"of forest and make hunting easier.","h":0.01606554858452458},{"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"w":0.8069815063476562,"t":"Shipton's team's excavation of the shelters at the Kelo site unearthed a volcanic glass","x":0.080082135506870225,"y":0.32122093004070418},{"t":"substance called obsidian, which must have been brought over from another island, as","y":0.33988576305419049,"w":0.81532857259114588,"h":0.019742287154746352,"x":0.08001989179612394,"c":1},{"h":0.017456438407785546,"y":0.35899704993462178,"t":"there is no known source on Obi. It also revealed particular types of beads, similar to","c":1,"w":0.79671457926432288,"x":0.080082135369494545},{"t":"those previously found on islands in southern Wallacea. These finds again support the","x":0.080014450653470792,"h":0.019179964768851421,"w":0.80916539510091134,"c":1,"y":0.37508496093337673},{"x":0.078028745551882203,"h":0.01605697339263279,"w":0.54414784749348966,"c":1,"t":"idea that Obi islanders routinely travelled to other islands.","y":0.3952802357887959},{"h":0.016224188790560423,"t":"The excavations suggest people successfully lived in the two Kelo shelters for about","x":0.080082147901610487,"c":1,"y":0.43008849548154693,"w":0.79260777791341142},{"c":1,"t":"10,000 years. But then, about 8,000 years ago, both were abandoned. Did the residents","x":0.080016244140574511,"w":0.82765879313151047,"y":0.44644773783345371,"h":0.020228553029288165},{"w":0.81737701416015629,"c":1,"t":"leave Obi completely, or move elsewhere on the island? Perhaps the jungle had grown","x":0.077967194526050318,"h":0.020359329628733325,"y":0.46418462686555639},{"w":0.80903493245442704,"h":0.015988371857499573,"c":1,"x":0.080082123037272107,"t":"so thick that axes were no longer a match for the dense undergrowth. Perhaps people","y":0.48401162802173325},{"w":0.74537989298502605,"x":0.08008212745250641,"h":0.017441860412777621,"t":"simply moved to the coast and turned to fishing rather than hunting as a means","y":0.50145348838046455,"c":1},{"h":0.016559714483300514,"x":0.079662932728906621,"y":0.51993039014551024,"c":1,"t":"of survival.","w":0.10567913691202799},{"x":0.080082136096583934,"y":0.55516224170243766,"w":0.82135523478190109,"t":"Whatever the reason for the departure, there is no evidence for use of the Kelo shelters","c":1,"h":0.017512176873761276},{"t":"after this time, until about 1,000 years ago, when they were re-occupied by people who","w":0.81736445109049483,"h":0.01877689642892133,"c":1,"y":0.57227202192061677,"x":0.080028746105833007},{"x":0.080082135408155092,"t":"owned pottery as well as items made out of gold and silver. It seems likely, in view of","y":0.58997050139216423,"h":0.017699115044247815,"c":1,"w":0.79671457926432299},{"h":0.017537044423871273,"y":0.60901162793082664,"c":1,"x":0.080082135054309819,"t":"Obi's location, that this final phase of occupation also saw the Kelo shelters used by","w":0.78850102742513017},{"y":0.62645348848748972,"t":"people involved in the historic trade in spices between the Maluku islands and the rest of","c":1,"x":0.080082130219260347,"h":0.016024387550916619,"w":0.83572896321614587},{"c":1,"t":"the world.","w":0.098839441935221345,"y":0.64486298670468845,"h":0.015506584595086692,"x":0.07789034078205298},{"w":0.03080082257588701,"c":1,"y":0.91715116283578513,"h":0.015988371857499684,"t":"63","x":0.88706365431780587},{"y":0.94166666658950615,"x":0.51176469618764042,"w":0.45882354736328113,"c":1,"h":0.04166666666666663,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}]}